def prod_signs(arr):
    arr = list(set(arr))     # remove duplicates
    arr = [x for x in arr if x != 0]  # remove zeros

    product = 1
    for num in arr:
        product *= num

    if product > 0:
        return "Positive"
    elif product < 0:
        return "Negative"
    else:
        return "Zero"
```

This function first turns the array into a set to remove duplicates, then list comprehension is used to remove any zeros. After that, it calculates the product of the remaining elements in the array. It then checks the sign of the product and returns a corresponding string.

The resulting "prod_signs" function will now only consider unique, non-zero integers from an array and will return whether the product of these integers is positive, negative or zero. Remember to check for an empty array after removing duplicates and zeros, as this may throw an error if not handled.

